KNOWNBUG
type_pack.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ sizeof of each type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold]/2, [temp.variadic]/5: in `(0 + ... + sizeof(Ts))'
the pack is the template's TYPE parameter pack, not a function parameter
pack; each element is sizeof of one type.  The function-body fold
expansion only expands function parameter packs, so the value is wrong.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.  Pre-existing.
